WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.030 --> 00:00:05.130
We just got the first awesome trailer for
Black Panther which gives us a glorious peek

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:09.250
inside the world of Wakanda and a first look
at new villains in the MCU.

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:13.719
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here
and in this video, I'm breaking down the Black

00:00:13.719 --> 00:00:16.980
Panther trailer for easter eggs, references
and other teases for what we can look forward

00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:18.790
to seeing in the movie.

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:23.070
The trailer kicks off with the return of Ulysses
Klaue and he's missing his left arm which

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:27.150
you'll probably remember he lost when Ultron
cut it off in Avengers: Age of Ultron.

00:00:27.150 --> 00:00:31.730
Klaue was stockpiling vibranium which he sold
to Ultron in that movie and here he's being

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:36.679
interrogated by Everett Ross, the CIA op who
appeared for the first time in Captain America:

00:00:36.679 --> 00:00:37.720
Civil War.

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:42.030
In the comics, Klaue also loses a limb and
gets a prosthetic arm equipped with a sonic

00:00:42.030 --> 00:00:45.010
emitter that he uses as a weapon, and I'll
talk more about that later.

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:48.899
By the way, I'm sure it won't be lost on fans
of The Hobbit that, thanks to this scene,

00:00:48.899 --> 00:00:52.149
we're seeing Bilbo Baggins and Gollum together
again!

00:00:52.149 --> 00:00:56.050
Next up is this misty shot of an enormous
waterfall which reminded me of the last time

00:00:56.050 --> 00:01:00.190
we saw Black Panther in the mid-credits scene
for Captain America: Civil War when T'Challa

00:01:00.190 --> 00:01:05.050
and Steve Rogers looked out over a jungle
landscape with a waterfall in the distance.

00:01:05.050 --> 00:01:09.119
This is actually Warrior Falls and in the
following shots we'll see T'Challa emerging

00:01:09.119 --> 00:01:12.490
from his Royal Talon Fighter for his coronation
ceremony.

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:16.659
You no doubt noticed T'Challa's fantastic
tattoos as he steps out of his craft and it's

00:01:16.659 --> 00:01:20.189
a little difficult to see here, but they're
actually panther-themed.

00:01:20.189 --> 00:01:24.320
And greeting T'Challa for the ceremony is
Forest Whitaker who is playing Zuri, a spiritual

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:27.160
leader and a father-like figure to T'Challa.

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:31.290
Director Ryan Coogler has described Zuri as
an Obi-Wan Kenobi-type character who will

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:34.250
advise and guide Black Panther in the movie.

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:38.450
And with Zuri you can also see these children
preparing for the ceremonial ritual.

00:01:38.450 --> 00:01:40.810
They're using something called the Heart-Shaped
Herb.

00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:44.880
In the comics, the juices of this herb are
prepared in a ceremony and given only to those

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:47.180
who are worthy enough to become the Black
Panther.

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:51.850
The herb gives the receiver super-strength,
speed, agility, senses and healing powers

00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:54.740
which you can see in some of the awesome action
shots in the trailer.

00:01:54.740 --> 00:01:59.289
Notice, for example, the force with which
T'Challa slams this guy into a truck and the

00:01:59.289 --> 00:02:01.430
incredible back-flips in this shot.

00:02:01.430 --> 00:02:05.780
And the way Black Panther's vibranium armour
just deflects these bullets reminds me of

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:10.330
that rooftop scene in Civil War where bullets
also just glanced off him.

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:13.660
Also in the trailer we get one of our new
villains: Erik Killmonger, who's actually

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:17.990
the guy behind the mask breaking Klaue out
from his detention with a team of mercs.

00:02:17.990 --> 00:02:22.190
Killmonger is a supervillain and a powerful
nemesis of Black Panther, and the mask he's

00:02:22.190 --> 00:02:25.920
wearing here is a bit different from the one
he has in the comics, though it retains the

00:02:25.920 --> 00:02:27.599
mane around the mask.

00:02:27.599 --> 00:02:31.720
Erik Killmonger is played by Michael B. Jordan
who worked with Black Panther director Ryan

00:02:31.720 --> 00:02:36.430
Coogler previously on Creed and Fruitvale
Station, and we can see Killmonger apprehended

00:02:36.430 --> 00:02:40.989
later in the trailer and escorted by W'Kabi
who is T'Challa's chief of security in the

00:02:40.989 --> 00:02:41.989
comics.

00:02:41.989 --> 00:02:46.660
W'Kabi is played by Daniel Kaluuya who recently
starred in the horror movie Get Out.

00:02:46.660 --> 00:02:50.480
And it looks like Killmonger has been escorted
to meet T'Challa and the other tribal leaders

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:51.879
in this throne room.

00:02:51.879 --> 00:02:56.010
By the way, this tribal leader with a lip
plate is currently described on IMDB as a

00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:57.010
River Tribe Elder.

00:02:57.010 --> 00:03:02.290
There's a number of T'Challa's elite female
bodyguards, the Dora Milaje, in the trailer.

00:03:02.290 --> 00:03:07.099
Overseeing the interrogation of Klaue is Okoye,
played by Danai Gurira from The Walking Dead.

00:03:07.099 --> 00:03:11.121
And there's this very cool group shot of the
Dora Milaje headed up by Florence Kasumba.

00:03:11.121 --> 00:03:16.810
Kasumba appeared briefly in Captain America:
Civil War where she faced off with Black Widow,

00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:19.370
telling the Avenger to move or be moved.

00:03:19.370 --> 00:03:24.000
Back to this trailer, in the casino scene
is Nakia, played by Lupita Nyong'o and she

00:03:24.000 --> 00:03:28.900
also appears later in her Dora Milaje outfit
with some cool disc-like weapons.

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:33.700
And next to Nakia is Shuri, T'Challa's sister,
played by Letitia Wright, and she's sporting

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:35.739
some very cool Panther-style blasters.

00:03:35.739 --> 00:03:40.250
These are likely a vibranium-based weapon
that she's developed herself, because her

00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:44.230
background in the movie is that she's spent
many years researching vibranium and developing

00:03:44.230 --> 00:03:45.230
technology.

00:03:45.230 --> 00:03:48.829
Which makes me wonder if Klaue will be trying
to steal some of her tech for his weaponised

00:03:48.829 --> 00:03:49.849
prosthetic arm?

00:03:49.849 --> 00:03:54.209
Nakia and Shuri also show up again in this
scene with T'Challa's mother Ramonda.

00:03:54.209 --> 00:03:58.580
This shot is set in the mountain terrain of
the Jabari tribe and another scene introduces

00:03:58.580 --> 00:04:01.470
their leader M'Baku, also known in the comics
as Man-Ape.

00:04:01.470 --> 00:04:06.310
M'Baku is a powerful tribal leader who's been
a long-standing enemy of Black Panther in

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:07.310
the comics.

00:04:07.310 --> 00:04:11.849
His comic book character led the outlawed
White Gorilla cult and he obtained super-strength

00:04:11.849 --> 00:04:15.280
after taking part in a ritual involving a
white gorilla.

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:19.470
And you can see a little nod to that perhaps
in the white fur he and his followers are

00:04:19.470 --> 00:04:20.470
wearing.

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:23.880
Now, this is an interesting shot, because
look carefully at the spokes on Black Panther's

00:04:23.880 --> 00:04:28.000
collar and they're definitely different to
the ones we saw him wear in Captain America:

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:30.500
Civil War and earlier in the trailer.

00:04:30.500 --> 00:04:34.630
I'm curious as to whether this is a flashback,
an early version of his suit or perhaps his

00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:37.830
suit's been damaged and he's had to go back
to an earlier prototype.

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:42.020
So, what did you think of the Black Panther
trailer and did it get you hyped up for the

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:43.020
movie?

00:04:43.020 --> 00:04:45.039
And were there any other easter eggs or cool
details you noticed?

00:04:45.039 --> 00:04:47.800
I'd love to hear your thoughts in the comments
below.

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:51.340
If you enjoyed this, you might also like my
Wonder Woman easter eggs video where I've

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:54.590
got a cool giveaway for an awesome art of
the movie book.

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:58.180
And don't forget to give this video a thumbs-up
if you liked it and while you're here check

00:04:58.180 --> 00:05:01.360
out some of my other videos by tapping or
clicking the screen.

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:03.150
Thanks for watching and see ya next time!

